  "title": "The Empty Seat Sketch",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "silent emotional stories",
  "premise": "A sketch artist wants to draw a two-person picnic, but the second seat stays empty and every attempt to erase it leaves a mark. They turn the mark into a flower growing beside the seat and finish a drawing that has room for both absence and today’s sunshine.",
  "hook": "The seat stays.",
  "visible_action": "Pencil traces two chairs; eraser rubs one pale mark; a stem grows from it; artist colors a small flower and closes the sketchbook gently.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "A picture can hold an absence without hiding it.",
  "gate": "Treat the absent person’s reason as unspecified; do not claim that a creative act resolves grief or mental-health needs.",
